  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass 1 kg is pushed up a surface inclined to horizontal at an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ by a force of 10 N parallel to the inclined surface as shown in figure. When the block is pushed up by 10 m along inclined surface, the work done against frictional force is :\n$\\left[g=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2\\right]$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/X2qT35fN71-1LXR_N9Lc_RAGBzAe6_y9rXaY6bA0HFo.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iCbqV",
      "text": "$5 \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WSX0F",
      "text": "5 J",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xffLL",
      "text": "$5 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "usfIh",
      "text": "10 J",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Mass of block, $m=1 \\mathrm{~kg}$\nForce of parallel inclined surface, $\\mathrm{F}=10 \\mathrm{~N}$\nWork done against frictional force\n$=\\mu_2 \\mathrm{~N} \\times 10=\\mu \\mathrm{Mg} \\cos 60 \\times 10=0.1 \\times 5 \\times 10=5 \\mathrm{~J}$",
    "image": null
  },
